{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "008R", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "\\begin{eqnarray*}\n\\Mor_{\\textit{Mod}(\\mathcal{O})}(\n\\mathcal{O} \\otimes_{f^{-1}f_*\\mathcal{O}} f^{-1}\\mathcal{G}, \\mathcal{F})\n& = &\n\\Mor_{\\textit{Mod}(f^{-1}f_*\\mathcal{O})}(\nf^{-1}\\mathcal{G}, \\mathcal{F}_{f^{-1}f_*\\mathcal{O}}) \\\\\n& = &\n\\Mor_{\\textit{Mod}(f_*\\mathcal{O})}(\\mathcal{G}, f_*\\mathcal{F}).\n\\end{eqnarray*}", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-adjointness-tensor-restrict}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-adjoint-push-pull-modules}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e579a31c72510daa22c8904da43114a385e9f00159e0f56a2fe4673bf8e81546", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:19c61b0853ec1235cc7c30e3a0a08fd9d63cd4b977ce7d6e42862ba8aed5ce88", "source_text": "This follows from the equalities\n<MATH_0001>\nwhich are a combination of\nLemma <REF_0001>\nand <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:785610b8772ade21f9c378c3f016f9ef2c9cac5cd00f066231fb5b251f03ca53", "unit_id": "tag:008Z:proof"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "008R", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}_Y$", "MATH_0005": "$Y$", "MATH_0006": "\\begin{eqnarray*}\nf_* : \\textit{PMod}(\\mathcal{O}_X) &\n\\longrightarrow &\n\\textit{PMod}(f_*\\mathcal{O}_X) \\\\\nf_* : \\textit{Mod}(\\mathcal{O}_X) &\n\\longrightarrow &\n\\textit{Mod}(f_*\\mathcal{O}_X) \\\\\nf_p : \\textit{PMod}(\\mathcal{O}_Y) &\n\\longrightarrow &\n\\textit{PMod}(f_p\\mathcal{O}_Y) \\\\\nf^{-1} : \\textit{Mod}(\\mathcal{O}_Y) &\n\\longrightarrow &\n\\textit{Mod}(f^{-1}\\mathcal{O}_Y)\n\\end{eqnarray*}", "MATH_0007": "$(f_*, f^{-1})$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{O}_X, \\mathcal{O}_Y$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{O}_X = f^{-1}\\mathcal{O}_Y$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{O}_Y = f_*\\mathcal{O}_X$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:cbda069734eeef8b937722951ed800b3c0cd80df2bdad86331f42cea525dcd50", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f25b4eca5712ed3e12c970417ad01ce2c22a36137c345eab4a813edccf085fdd", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a continuous map.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a (pre)sheaf of rings on <MATH_0003> and\nlet <MATH_0004> be a (pre)sheaf of rings on <MATH_0005>.\nSo at the moment we have defined functors\n<MATH_0006>\nClearly, usually the pair of functors <MATH_0007>\non sheaves of modules are not adjoint, because their target categories\ndo not match. Namely, as we saw above, it works only if by some miracle the\nsheaves of rings <MATH_0008> satisfy the\nrelations <MATH_0009> and\n<MATH_0010>. This is almost never\ntrue in practice. We interrupt the discussion to define\nthe correct notion of morphism for which a suitable adjoint\npair of functors on sheaves of modules exists.\n\n", "source_text_hash